Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Solvetus Labs <info@solvetus.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Solvetus/pervius-app
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1, gir1.2-nm-1.0, gir1.2-secret-1, gir1.2-soup-3.0, network-manager, network-manager-openvpn, openvpn, nftables, polkitd, dbus-broker | dbus-daemon | dbus, systemd
Conflicts: solvetus-vpn, solvetus-vpn-killswitch
Replaces: solvetus-vpn, solvetus-vpn-killswitch
Provides: solvetus-vpn, solvetus-vpn-killswitch
Description: unofficial Linux client for FastVPN
 Pervius is a GTK 4/libadwaita desktop client for an existing FastVPN
 (OpenVPN) subscription. It validates the provider's public server
 catalogue and imports profiles through NetworkManager and its OpenVPN
 plugin. The application runs as an ordinary user; NetworkManager performs
 privileged network operations.
 .
 The package also installs an optional kill-switch system service and CLI.
 The service is idle until explicitly armed through polkit; the GUI remains
 unprivileged.
 .
 Pervius is an independent open-source project by Solvetus Labs. It is not
 affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Namecheap, Inc. FastVPN is a
 trademark of Namecheap, Inc.
